    <GaugingStation location="Loddiswell" name="Avon" number="46008">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station with natural control to 2013, weir thereafter.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Cableway present, span 25.5m. Minimal bypassing. Pre-weir low flows were affected by weed growth and movement of the natural bed control (downstream of station) causing frequent re-rating. Reasonable fit to available gaugings.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity area station built in 1971. Natural control until Flat V weir built in 2012/13.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Station closed between 6/10/1981 - 11/05/1990. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2020 (WINFAP Files v9).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Some regulation from surface water and groundwater abstractions. Avon Dam in the catchment (small reservoir in the headwaters) can affect runoff. Dam fills quickly and overspills during significant events, but would make no difference to the flow at Loddiswell. Hydro-electric power scheme was installed at the Dam (in 2012), on the falling limb of events, flows can suddenly drop when the reservoir stops releasing.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Drains southwards from Dartmoor Granite. Predominantly Lower Old Red Sandstone in lower reaches, Culm Measures between. Alluvium in valley bottom. Land-use: rural, grazing and woodland in steeply incised valley. No major catchment changes.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">SR</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Gauged to just above QMED, but good fit to gaugings, some of which are for out of bank conditions." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
